---
import SubpageLayout from '../../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import ProcessSteps from '../../../components/blocks/ProcessSteps.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../../components/blocks/CardGrid.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/blocks/Callout.astro';
import StandardBand from '../../../components/blocks/StandardBand.astro';

const path = [
  { title: 'The start sprint', eyebrow: 'Week 1', body: 'One week, fixed fee. We sit down with the owner of the problem, build a prototype on your data or design the architecture, and put the business case on one page next to it. Then you decide.', href: '/en/start-sprint', hrefLabel: 'More about the start sprint' },
  { title: 'Business case and scoping', eyebrow: 'Before the build', body: 'What it costs, what it returns, when it pays back. Because we build ourselves, our estimates are realistic. If the business case does not add up, we do not build.', href: '/en/services/consulting', hrefLabel: 'How we make the business case' },
  { title: 'Build in sprints', eyebrow: 'Weeks 2 to 12', body: 'Short sprints with a demo at the end of each sprint, so you always see where we are. Independently or together with your developers. Connected to your ERP, CRM and the rest of your landscape.' },
  { title: 'Compliance from the drawing board', eyebrow: 'During the build', body: 'We classify the system under the AI Act, build in logging and human oversight and choose hosting that fits your data.' },
  { title: 'Training your team', eyebrow: 'Before the switch', body: 'We train the team that will use the system on that system, on the work floor. That also meets Article 4 of the EU AI Act.', href: '/en/services/training', hrefLabel: 'How we train' },
  { title: 'Handover without lock-in', eyebrow: 'Delivery', body: 'Source code, documentation and data model are yours. You can carry on without us if you want to. If you would rather not, we keep managing and developing it.' },
];

const principles = [
  { title: 'Working over finished', description: 'We measure success by what runs at handover, and by what still runs a year later.' },
  { title: 'Honesty over sales', description: 'If AI is not the solution, we say so. If the business case does not add up, we do not build.' },
  { title: 'Start small, then scale', description: 'First a week, then a decision, then a build. Never a large sum on a hunch.' },
  { title: 'We do what we advise', description: 'Our own assistant runs on this site, hosted in Europe. We automate our own work with what we build for clients.' },
];
---

<SubpageLayout
  lang="en"
  title="How we work"
  subtitle="From ambition to implementation. First a week, then a decision, then a build that works at handover."
  seoTitle="How we work: start sprint, business case, build, compliance, training, handover"
  seoDescription="How AI Heroes works: a start sprint of one week, a business case before the build, building in sprints, compliance from the drawing board, training your team and handover without lock-in. The AI Heroes standard, explained."
  accentColor="red"
  badge="How we work"
  showStandard={false}
>
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-dark mb-4">The problem we solve</h2>
    <p class="text-lg text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      The AI market is fragmented. Advisory firms write reports that end up in drawers. Training bureaus train and leave. Tech companies build tools nobody uses. Almost nobody delivers software that works on the day of delivery and keeps working.
    </p>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">That is why we build, and bring along everything that makes a build succeed: the business case before it, the compliance inside it and the training after it. It is what every build contains, rather than a menu to pick from.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-dark mb-6">The journey, in order</h2>
    <ProcessSteps steps={path} />
  </section>

  <StandardBand lang="en" id="standard" class="mb-16" />

  <section id="compliance" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-28">
    <Callout variant="dark" accent="blue" eyebrow="Compliance from the drawing board" title="What that means in practice">
      <p><strong>Classification.</strong> Every system we build gets a place under the AI Act: minimal, limited or high risk. That determines what has to be in the design.</p>
      <p><strong>Logging and oversight.</strong> Every decision the system makes can be traced, and a human can always step in. For an assistant that means handover to a person; for a workflow, a review step.</p>
      <p><strong>Hosting.</strong> Data that may not leave Europe stays in Europe. On your own servers if it has to be, with a European provider if it can be.</p>
      <p><strong>Literacy.</strong> The team that works with it is trained on the system. That means you meet Article 4, with the evidence to show for it.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-dark mb-6">What we hold ourselves to</h2>
    <CardGrid items={principles} cols={2} />
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-dark mb-4">What it costs</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">The start sprint costs from €8,000, fixed fee, known up front. A custom build after that starts from €15,000. What your build will cost exactly is on paper at the end of the start sprint, together with what it returns and when it pays back.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Standalone trainings are available too, from €2,500 per day; you will find them under <a href="/en/services/training" class="text-brand-red underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">training your team</a>. For education and non-profit organisations we apply lower rates.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <Callout variant="light" accent="red" eyebrow="Next step" title="Tell us what you want to build">
      <p>A start sprint is the first step. Below you can tell us what it is about; we respond within 24 hours.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>
</SubpageLayout>
